  <name>FirewallFabrik</name>
  <summary>Manage iptables and nftables policies for many firewalls</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      FirewallFabrik is the successor to Firewall Builder (fwbuilder). It manages the firewall policies of many Linux hosts from one data file: networks, hosts, services and rule sets are defined once as objects and reused in every firewall.
    </p>
    <p>
      For each firewall it generates a shell script for iptables or nftables that configures the interfaces and activates the policy, and installs it over SSH.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Policy, NAT and routing rule sets with drag and drop</li>
      <li>Clusters with shared and per-member rules</li>
      <li>Rules shadowed by an earlier rule are reported when compiling</li>
      <li>Opens Firewall Builder .fwb files</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">ch.linuxfabrik.firewallfabrik.desktop</launchable>

